  "limitations": [
    "shared data lasts for one document and retained layout owner",
    "document refresh performs one new server read",
    "independent fetch owners are not deduplicated",
    "there is no request registry, invalidation graph, retained query cache, or universal polling scheduler",
    "runtime routes require the deployment host to apply the generated rewrites",
    "runtime project and issue navigation uses native document navigation",
    "protected static HTML is a UX shell; API authorization is the security boundary",
    "push-navigation transport failures retain the current document for explicit retry; invalid documents and asset failures use native document fallback",
    "forms use native constraints and application-owned state; there is no field registry, proxy metadata graph, or form runtime",
    "dirty and touched metadata is explicit object and array state rather than dynamic field registration",
    "draft persistence is application-owned versioned storage plus one dependency effect; there is no wizard or autosave scheduler",
    "fetch uploads expose no upload progress; chunking, resume, background sync, and an upload runtime remain unsupported",
    "object-state collection roots require one direct static array field and immutable replacement; dynamic paths and mutation remain unsupported",
    "incremental loading allows two successful pages of two records and retains at most six unique projects; larger datasets require the separately measured 0.14.3 browser decision",
    "destructive confirmation uses the native dialog top layer; custom focus traps, portals, stacked modals, and animated presence remain unsupported",
    "non-modal project actions use native Popover and key-scoped ID references; custom positioning engines, menu roving focus, Portal/Slot reconciliation, and retained overlay trees remain unsupported",
    "notifications use one layout-owned queue and one sequential timeout; pause-on-hover, cross-document persistence, priorities, and a global scheduler remain unsupported"
  ],
